    "display_name": "Dance Styles and Genres",
    "teacher_markdown": "**What Students Should Take Away:**\r\n\r\n* Students should use a consistent process to evaluate, clean, and verify a dataset.\r\n* Students should use `replace()`, `fillna()`, or `drop()` based on the type of data-quality issue and its context.\r\n* Students should recheck the cleaned dataset and visualization to confirm that their changes worked.\r\n\r\n**Misconceptions Students Might Have or Points They Might Struggle With and Tips to Assist:**\r\n\r\n* Students may try to clean every column instead of focusing on the columns identified in the starter code.\r\n\r\n  * Tip: Direct students to complete the required focus columns before investigating additional issues.\r\n* Students may struggle to decide whether to replace, fill, or drop data.\r\n\r\n  * Tip: Encourage students to consider whether a value can be corrected and how removing or replacing it could affect the analysis.\r\n* Students may modify the original `data` DataFrame instead of `data_cleaned`.\r\n\r\n  * Tip: Remind students to apply each cleaning step to the copy so they can compare the original and cleaned data.\r\n* Students may assume the dataset is clean when the program runs without an error.\r\n\r\n  * Tip: Have students repeat their missing-value checks, unique-value checks, and bar chart after cleaning.\r\n* Students may rely on AI Tutor to make cleaning decisions for them.\r\n\r\n  * Tip: Encourage students to use AI Tutor to explain code, documentation, output, or errors, then make their own decisions based on the dataset.\r\n",
